                          <h3 style={{ fontSize: 14, margin: '0 0 8px' }}>Nuclear structure & isotope</h3>
                          <p style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#c4d8e8', lineHeight: 1.7, margin: 0 }}>
                            Atomic number identifies the element and equals its proton count. The displayed neutron count is estimated from the database's common mass number; isotopes of this element can have different neutron counts.
                          </p>
                        </div>

                        <div style={{ marginTop: 16 }}>
                          <h3 style={{ fontSize: 14, margin: '0 0 8px' }}>Chemical overview</h3>
                          <p style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#c4d8e8', lineHeight: 1.7, margin: 0 }}>
                            Category: {selectedElement.category}. Group and period describe the element's position in the periodic table and help explain trends in valence electrons and chemical behaviour. Specific oxidation states and reactivity depend on the element and its compounds.
                          </p>
                        </div>
                      </>
                    ) : selectedModel === 'Neural Network' ? (
                      <>
                        {[
                          ['Architecture', 'Layered computational model'],
                          ['Input layer', 'Receives features or input values'],
                          ['Hidden layers', 'Learn intermediate representations'],
                          ['Output layer', 'Produces prediction or classification'],
                          ['Neuron', 'Computes a weighted sum plus bias, then applies an activation function'],
                          ['Weights', 'Trainable parameters that scale connections'],
                          ['Biases', 'Trainable offsets applied to neuron inputs'],
                          ['Forward propagation', 'Passes values through the network to calculate outputs'],
